Follow-up — namespaced consumer hook groups, 2026-10-13:
- Pinned Java Push/Pull/Lite startup wraps the facade consumer group with the configured namespace; each `ConsumeMessageContext.consumerGroup` receives that wrapped group. Rust previously passed the unwrapped config value in all three hook contexts.
- Push context construction now uses the validated namespace to produce the effective group; Pull hook execution propagates namespace-resolution errors and uses its effective consumer group; Lite poll builds the same group before invoking hooks. The matrix records the three paths. Lite custom hook registration remains crate-private because `DefaultLitePullConsumer` has no public user-registration method.
- Extended the Push, Pull, and Lite hook lifecycle tests with a `tenant` namespace and exact `tenant%<group>` expectations.
- Validation: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --locked` PASS (149 unit tests and 35 integration tests); `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings` PASS. Workspace-wide gates remain pending.

Follow-up — synchronous channel callback isolation, 2026-10-13:
- Read the pinned `NettyRemotingAbstract.NettyEventExecutor`: Java dispatches channel callbacks serially on its own service thread after bounded queue admission. Rust's owned event queue still invoked synchronous callbacks directly on a Tokio worker; a blocking `on_connect` callback could stall even a current-thread runtime and transport progress.
- Added `p16_slow_sync_channel_observer_does_not_block_transport_runtime`. It failed before the change because the Tokio runtime stalled until the synchronous callback's watchdog expired. Channel callbacks now execute serially via `spawn_blocking`; async Active work is driven on that blocking worker and still observes shutdown cancellation. The trait documents queue-overflow and non-preemptible synchronous callback behavior.
- Validation PASS: the new single-thread runtime transport regression, `async_active_listener_is_owned_panic_isolated_and_cancelled_on_shutdown`, `p16_slow_channel_observer_does_not_block_transport_and_is_cancelled_on_shutdown`, and `p16_channel_events_carry_connection_generation_and_redacted_peer`. Workspace gates remain pending.

